# Paths this project keeps in the working tree and never commits. Each is here because a
#   build or a test needs it present, not because it is ours to publish -- so `git add` on
#   the project directory cannot sweep them in, which is exactly what it did once.
#   The repository root's own `.gitignore` already drops extensionless build products (`*`
#   re-included by `!*.*`), so only the files carrying an extension ever reached this far.
#   Whole directories are named rather than suffixes, so that stays a detail of how Nim
#   names its output rather than something to rediscover.
#   Unlike `dependencies.list`, this format has **no inline comments**: a trailing `# ...`
#   is part of the pattern, and a rule written that way silently matches nothing.

# Build output, both binaries and the generated browser page; `tools/verify.sh` rebuilds it.
/bin/

# Vendored PGA library, under Prosperity 3.0.0. Kept locally so builds and tests run, never
#   staged; PROVENANCE.md records where it came from, at which commit, and under what terms.
/pga.nim
/pga/

# Vendored WOFF2 faces under OFL-1.1, embedded into the browser page at build time.
/fonts/

# Dear ImGui checkout, under the MIT licence, compiled straight into the desktop binary
#   rather than linked; `dependencies.list` carries the clone command and `gui.nim` the
#   path it expects. PROVENANCE.md has always named it among the paths the working tree
#   carries and the repository does not; it was the one of the four missing from here.
/deps/
